 ],
 "literal": "O wise-mouthed Vēlaṉ who rejoiced in performing worship to Murukaṉ! / Avoid getting angry, I have something to ask. / Along with food offerings of a few cooked rice grains of many different colors, / having killed a small kid, having stroked her fragrant forehead, / if you bow and give the offering, / will this sacrificial offering also eat the bright-garlanded chest / of the lord of the mountain slopes of the great sky-touching mountain, who afflicted her?",
 "translation": "O wise Vēlaṉ, who rejoices in performing worship to Murukaṉ! Do not be angry, for I have a question to ask. If you sacrifice a young kid, stroke her fragrant forehead, bow down, and present the food offering of various colors, will that sacrifice also consume the chest, adorned with a bright garland, of the lord of the high, sky-touching mountain slopes—the one who actually caused her distress?",
 "modern": "முருகனை வழிபட்டு மகிழும் அறிவுமிக்க வேலனே! என்மீது கோபப்படாமல் இரு; நான் உன்னிடம் ஒன்று கேட்க வேண்டும். பல வண்ணங்களையுடைய சில சோற்று உருண்டைகளுடன், சிறிய ஆட்டுக்குட்டியைக் கொன்று, இவளுடைய நறிய நெற்றியைத் தடவி, நீ வணங்கிப் பலியைக் கொடுத்தால், இவளுக்குத் துன்பத்தைத் தந்த, மேகங்கள் தொடும் பெரிய மலைநாட்டிற்குரிய தலைவனுடைய ஒளிபொருந்திய மாலை அணிந்த மார்பையும் அந்தப் பலி ஏற்குமோ?",
 "explanation": "The confidante is speaking to the Vēlaṉ, the priest of Murukaṉ, who has been called by the heroine's mother to perform a ritual sacrifice to cure her daughter's mysterious illness. The mother mistakenly believes her daughter is possessed by Murukaṉ, whereas she is actually suffering from love-sickness due to separation from her lover. The confidante politely asks the priest not to get angry and poses a sharp, ironic question. She asks if the sacrificial offering of a young goat and colored rice will also consume or satisfy the chest of the mountain lord who actually caused her distress. Through this question, she subtly reveals the true cause of the heroine's illness to the family, indicating that only union with the hero can cure her.",
